<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;THE CROWN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Crown is a television series known for its historical drama, particularly focusing on the reign of Queen Elizabeth II."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOURTH-SEASON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The fourth season of The Crown is a significant event in the series, marking a continuation of the narrative."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOVEMBER 15, 2020&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"November 15, 2020 is the premiere date for the fourth season of The Crown."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OCTOBER 13, 2020&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"October 13, 2020 is the date when news about the premiere and cast changes for the fourth season were revealed."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOVEMBER 15, 2012&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"November 15, 2012 is mentioned in another context, possibly referring to a different event or release date."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLD OPEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The cold open of the fourth season is a significant event, setting the tone for the premiere."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLEAK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bleak describes the mood and tone of the fourth-season premiere, indicating a somber and serious atmosphere."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2020&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"YEAR"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2020 is also mentioned as the current year during the events described."&lt;SEP&gt;"2020 is the year in which the events and announcements about the fourth season take place."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURFACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surface refers to the initial impression or appearance of the fourth-season premiere, which is described as bleak."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREMIERE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Premiere refers to the official start of the fourth season, which took place on November 15, 2020."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAST CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cast changes are mentioned as part of the news revealed on October 13, 2020."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEWS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"News about the fourth season, including the premiere date and cast changes, were revealed on October 13, 2020."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHOTOS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ARTIFACT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Photos from the fourth season were recently revealed, providing visual evidence of the upcoming premiere."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Changes refer to the modifications in the cast for the fourth season, which were announced on October 13, 2020."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANNOUNCEMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Announcements about the fourth season, including the premiere date and cast changes, were made on October 13, 2020."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRAMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Drama refers to the genre of the series, which is known for its historical and dramatic elements."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUEEN ELIZABETH II&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Queen Elizabeth II is the subject of the historical drama series, The Crown."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HISTORICAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Historical refers to the nature of the series, which focuses on the reign of Queen Elizabeth II."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NARRATIVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Narrative refers to the ongoing storylines and events in the series, particularly the fourth season."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REIGN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reign refers to the period of rule of Queen Elizabeth II, which is the focus of the series."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TELEVISION SERIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TYPE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Television series refers to the format of the show, which is broadcast on television."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TELEVISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MEDIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Television refers to the medium through which the series is distributed and viewed."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANNOUNCED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Announced refers to the act of revealing information about the fourth season, such as the premiere date and cast changes."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SERIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TYPE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Series refers to the ongoing nature of the show, which continues with each new season."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW SEASON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"New season refers to the introduction of the fourth season, which is a significant event in the series."</data>
      <data key="d2">rgb-0054</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;THE CROWN&quot;" target="&quot;FOURTH-SEASON&quot;">
